    {
      "id": "one",
      "name": "Gudial",
      "description": "The head goes dark and takes an intricate striped mask around the eyes and muzzle. Bold upright bands cross the neck, and the legs are banded the whole way down to the hoof - segmented, high-contrast, deliberately loud. Along the back and barrel is a scatter of spotting. All of it is one gradient rather than one colour: the marking sweeps between two hues from the nose to the tail, so the face stripes and the hindquarter spotting are visibly different colours and everything between them is on the way from one to the other. Which two, and how far apart, run in the line. The mane carries no regular striping and the hooves take the colour of their end of the sweep.",
